<title>USA: Biocontrol says submits test data to FDA.</title>
<headline>Biocontrol says submits test data to FDA.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biocontrol Technology Inc said Wednesday it has submitted to the Food and Drug Administration preliminary data from in-home testing on its noninvasive glucose sensor for diabetics.</p>
<p>The in-home testing of the sensor, called Diasensor1000, was required by the FDA and is part of the overall approval process necessary to market it.</p>
<p>The company said at-home use produced better results than use of the system at calibration centers.</p>
</text>
